      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitballard.com/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Ballard’s first wagon bridge opened in 1889, followed by the first railroad bridge in 1890, linking the town to Seattle.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ballardhistory.org/mapping-ballard-new/ballard-overview/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Ballard Historical Society, a volunteer non‑profit, runs self‑guided tours and preserves archives but has no traditional museum space.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
